From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Subject: Input: melfas_mip4 - mirror a missing axis resolution (J701F local)

Written by Claude 2026-10-09 for the J701F project; not an upstream patch.
Applies after linux-mip4-vdd-supply.patch (file name sorts last on purpose).
The MMS438 reports ppm_x = 10 and ppm_y = 0; KWin's libinput logs "kernel has
only x or y resolution, not both" and ignores the device.
---
--- a/drivers/input/touchscreen/melfas_mip4.c
+++ b/drivers/input/touchscreen/melfas_mip4.c
@@ -335,6 +335,15 @@
 
 		ts->ppm_x = buf[12];
 		ts->ppm_y = buf[13];
+		/*
+		 * J701F local: this panel reports only an X resolution.
+		 * libinput rejects a touchscreen with one resolution set
+		 * and the other zero, so mirror the one that is known.
+		 */
+		if (!ts->ppm_y)
+			ts->ppm_y = ts->ppm_x;
+		else if (!ts->ppm_x)
+			ts->ppm_x = ts->ppm_y;
 		dev_dbg(&ts->client->dev, "ppm_x: %d, ppm_y: %d\n",
 			ts->ppm_x, ts->ppm_y);
 
